             "onupdate",
             "callback function that updates the accessory aggregation state.  @param state the accessory aggregation state.",
             "getfileliststate",
             "current file list state of the speaker.  @return an enum value of `fileliststate`.",
             "getdatatransmissionstate",
             "the data transmission state of the speaker.  @return an enum value of `speakerdatatransmissionstate`.",
             "setvolume",
             "sets the volume to play audio. the valid range is [0, 100]. 100 means loudest.  @param value volume value to set. @param callback the execution callback with the returned execution result.",
             "setplaymode",
             "sets the play mode of the speaker to control the behavior after finishing playing a file.  @param mode the play mode to set. @param callback the execution callback with the returned execution result.",
             "starttransmission",
             "starts to send a complete audio file to the aircraft, which can be played by the speaker.  a transmission session can only be started when the transmission state is in `idle`.  if the transmission is started successfully, the state will change  to `ready_to_transmit`. then  call `pacedata` to send data to sdk.  call `markeof` when all data has been sent to sdk. sdk will maintain a  buffer to hold all the data and transmit it to the aircraft. for m2e speaker, the audio file to transmit  should fulfill the following configurations:  - the speaker only receives raw pcm(pulse-code modulation) data of an audio file,  if the audio file is compressed, pcm extraction is needed before the transmission.  - the audio channel is mono.  -  the audio sample rate is 44,100 hz.  - the pcm (pulse-code modulation) sample  depth is 16 bit per sample.  - the audio file is stored in the aircraft instead  of the speaker.  @param info the information of the file to transmit. it is also used to determine the  location the file will be stored in the aircraft. @param listener inform the progress of the data transfer.",
             "pacedata",
             "sends raw pcm data of the audio file to sdk internal logic.  for mavic 2 enterprise, the transmission rate is limited to 80kb/s by sdk.  therefore, sdk will cache the paced data to a local file when the rate of pacing data is over 80kb/s. the paced data will be appended  to the local file. call `markeof` when all data of the data has been paced to sdk.  @param data raw pcm data stream in bytes.  @return `true` if data is paced successfully. otherwise, pacing data is not in the current state or the data size is illegal.",
             "markeof",
             "marks eof (end-of-file). it is used to inform sdk that all data of the file has been paced. sdk will continue  to transmit data to the aircraft. the state will change to `idle` when all data is transmitted.  after calling this method, `pacedata` is invalid until a new transmission session starts. if no  data is paced before calling this method, the transmission session will end immediately.  @return the occurred error if any.",
             "canceltransmission",
             "this will entirely stop the data transfer process and of course clean the transfer thread pool.",
             "play",
             "starts to play the audio file with the specific index.  @param fileindex the file index of the `audiomediafile` to play. @param callback the execution callback with the returned execution result.",
             "stop",
             "stops the speaker from playing audio. the method is only valid when  the playing state is `playing`.  @param callback the execution callback with the returned execution result.",
             "rename",
             "renames the audio file with the specific index. if the operation is started successfully, fileliststate will become `renaming`.  @param index the index of the audio file to rename. @param filename the new file name of the audio file. the file name should not exceed 128 characters. @param callback completion callback to receive the result.",
             "getfilelistsnapshot",
             "returns a copy of the current audio file list from the storage. returns `null` if `getfileliststate` is reset.  @return an array of `audiomediafile` objects.",
             "refreshfilelist",
             "refresh the audio file list in the aircraft.  - if the current state  is `reset`, sdk  will try to fetch the complete file list.  - if the current state is `incomplete`, sdk  will only fetch the missing list of files.  - if the operation is started successfully,  the `fileliststate`  will become `syncing`.  - when the  file list is refreshed successfully, the `fileliststate` will become `up_to_date`.  @param callback completion callback to receive the result.",
             "delete",
             "deletes audio files in the aircraft. if the operation is started successfully, `getfileliststate` will  become `deleting`. if there is error or  failedfiles is not empty, `getfileliststate`  will become `reset`.  @param fileindices a list of audiomediafile's index. @param callback completion callback to receive the result.",
             "addfileliststatelistener",
