             "waypointv2action",
             "this class represents an action for `waypointv2mission`. it determines how action is performed when a waypoint mission is executed.",
             "getactionid",
             "the id of action.  @return an int value of action id.",
             "gettrigger",
             "the trigger of action.  @return an object of `waypointtrigger`.",
             "getactuator",
             "the actuator of action.  @return an object of `waypointactuator`.",
             "builder",
             "the class is used to create the instance of `waypointv2action`.",
             "setactionid",
             "sets the action id.  @param actionid the value of action id.  @return the build of `builder`.",
             "settrigger",
             "sets the trigger.  @param trigger the object of `waypointtrigger`.  @return the build of `builder`.",
             "setactuator",
             "sets the actuator.  @param actuator the object of `waypointactuator`.  @return the build of `builder`.",
             "build",
             "create an object of `waypointv2action`.  @return the object of `waypointv2action`.",
             "intelligenthotpointmission",
             "this class represents an intelligent hotpoint mission. in an intelligent hotpoint mission, the aircraft will  repeatedly fly circles of a constant radius around a specified point called a hotpoint. the user can control  the aircraft to fly around the hotpoint with a specific radius and altitude. during execution, the user can  also use the physical remote controller to modify its radius and speed. it is only supported by mavic 2 zoom and mavic 2 pro.",
             "ispoimodeenabled",
             "`true` if poi mode is enabled. value is undefined if  the `getcurrentstate` is one of the  following:  - `not_supported`  - `disconnected`  - `recovering`.  now only  supported by mavic 2 zoom and mavic 2 pro.  @return a boolean value to check if poi mode is enabled.",
             "enablepoimode",
             "enable poi mode. enabling poi mode is the pre-condition of starting intelligent hotpoint mission.  now only supported by mavic 2 zoom and mavic 2 pro.  @param callback completioncallback callback that receives the execution result.",
             "disablepoimode",
             "disable poi mode. when poi mode is disabled, you can not starting intelligent hotpoint mission.  now only supported by mavic 2 zoom and mavic 2 pro.  @param callback completion callback that receives the execution result.",
             "getcurrentstate",
             "the current state of the executing intelligent hotpoint mission.  @return an object of `intelligenthotpointmissionstate`.",
             "addlistener",
             "adds listener to receive all of the intelligent hotpoint mission operator events.  @param listener listener that is interested in the intelligent hotpoint mission operator.",
             "removelistener",
             "removes listener. if the listener is listening to events and notifications, then it will stop listening to  all if called with this method.  @param targetlistener listener to be removed.",
             "removealllisteners",
             "remove all listeners from listener pool.",
             "startmission",
             "starts to execute an intelligent hotpoint mission. this only be called when the `getcurrentstate`  is `ready_to_start`. after a mission is started successfully, the `getcurrentstate` will become `executing`.  if the mission starts successful, the aircraft will fly arround the hotpoint of the mission. the current horizontal distance between the aircraft and the hotpoint must  be [5,500]. the current vertical distance between the aircraft and the relative takeoff altitude must be [5,500].  @param mission an object of `intelligenthotpointmission`. @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails to start the mission. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "startrecognizetargetinrect",
             "send a target rect in video stream to aircraft, the vision system will recognize the target in the rect. this only be called when  the `getcurrentstate` is `ready_to_start`.  after recognize target success, the `getcurrentstate` will become `waiting_for_confirmation`  means recognize the target successfully or `ready_to_start` means can not recognize the target.  @param rectf the tracking target rect in video stream. @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails to start recognize target. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "acceptconfirmation",
             "confirm the recognized target, only be called when the `getcurrentstate`  is `waiting_for_confirmation`. if accept successfully,  the `getcurrentstate` will become `measuring_target`,  the aircraft will measure the the target and calculate surrounding path. then the aircraft will start circle around the target on the surrounding path and `getcurrentstate`  will become `executing`.  @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "pausemission",
             "pauses the executing mission. it can only be called when the `getcurrentstate` is `executing`.  after a mission is paused successfully, the `getcurrentstate` will become `execution_paused`.  @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "resumemission",
             "resumes the paused mission. it can only be called when the `getcurrentstate`  is `execution_paused`. after a mission is resumed successfully,  the `getcurrentstate` will become `executing`.  @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "stopmission",
             "stops the executing or paused mission. it can only be called when `getcurrentstate` is one of the following:  - `executing`  - `execution_paused`  after a mission is stopped successfully, `getcurrentstate` will become `ready_to_start`.  @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "setangularvelocity",
             "sets angular velocity for the executing mission. it can only be called when `getcurrentstate` is one of the following:  - `executing`  - `execution_paused`  @param angularvelocity angular velocity to set. @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "setradius",
             "sets radius for the executing mission. it can only be called when the `getcurrentstate` is one of the  following:  - `executing`  - `execution_paused`  @param radius radius to set. @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "setaltitude",
             "sets altitude for the executing mission. it can only be called when the `getcurrentstate` is one of the following:  - `executing`  - `execution_paused`  @param altitude altitude to set. @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
             "resetgimbaltocenter",
             "reset gimbal to center for the executing mission, the camera will direct to the target. it can only be called when the `getcurrentstate` is one of the following:  - `executing`  - `execution_paused`  this feature is only avaliable in recognize mission.  @param callback completion callback that will be called when the operator succeeds or fails. if it fails, an error will be returned.",
