             "sdk key for getvoltage: returns the current battery voltage (mv).  @return an int value.",
             "getcurrent",
             "returns the real time current draw of the battery (ma). a negative value means the battery is being discharged, and a positive value means it is being charged.  @return an int value.",
             "current",
             "sdk key for getcurrent: returns the real time current draw of the battery (ma). a negative value means the battery is being discharged, and a positive value means it is being charged.  @return an int value.",
             "getlifetimeremaining",
             "returns the battery's remaining lifetime as a percentage, with range [0, 100]. a new battery will be close to 100%. as a battery experiences charge/discharge cycles, the value will go down. in unsupported products, this value will always be 0.  these products are phantom 4 pro, inspire 2, and phantom 4 advanced.  @return an int value.",
             "lifetime_remaining",
             "sdk key for getlifetimeremaining: returns the battery's remaining lifetime as a percentage, with range [0, 100]. a new battery will be close to 100%. as a battery experiences charge/discharge cycles, the value will go down. in unsupported products, this value will always be 0.  these products are phantom 4 pro, inspire 2, and phantom 4 advanced.  @return an int value.",
             "gettemperature",
             "returns the battery's temperature, in celsius, with range [-128, 127] degrees.  @return a float value.",
